217 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 405 0 R
/E (The train function is responsible for learning the link weights from the training data using backpropagation. It first uses the query function to calculate the hidden and output layer activation. After that, the error at the output layer is calculated and then propagated back to the hidden layer using the transpose of of the weights from hidden to output layer. The weights are then accordingly adjusted at the input using the gradient descent rule, which is:)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
